      "reasoning": "Turn 5! My Kavus are now 5/5 with the Island type from Steam Vents! Opponent is at 4 life (gained 2 from Dredger's Insight triggers). They added Badgermole Cub, a second Young Wolf, a second Dredger's Insight, and animated a Forest as a 1/1 creature.\n\
\n\
Their board has blockers: Young Wolf (1/1, not sick), Forest creature (1/1, tapped), Dryad Arbor (1/1, tapped), Badgermole Cub (2/2, summoning sick), Young Wolf #2 (1/1, summoning sick).\n\
\n\
So only one Young Wolf can block (the non-sick one, p28). It blocks one 5/5 Kavu. But 4 damage still gets through from the other Kavu = they're dead!\n\
\n\
Wait, I drew a second Leyline of the Guildpact! And I can also cast Scion of Draco for just 2 mana (12 - 10 = 2).\n\
\n\
Optimal plan: Just attack with both 5/5 Kavus. They can only block one with Young Wolf (1/1). The other 5/5 gets through = they take 5, going from 4 to -1. Dead!\n\
\n\
But wait, should I play Ragavan first? No need - Kavus alone win the game. Let me just go to combat.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me think if Scion of Draco would help. For 2 mana it gives all my creatures first strike + trample + vigilance + hexproof + lifelink. That's amazing if the opponent tries tricks, but I win this turn regardless. The trample means even if they block, damage tramples over.\n\
\n\
Let me play Scion of Draco for 2 mana first (gives trample, so even blocking is futile), then attack.",
